# Changelog: publishing a version

The app version lives in `FyneApp.toml` (`Version`, `Build`) and `version.go` (`Version`, no `v` prefix; a test
keeps both and the last `CHANGELOG.md` heading equal).

## 1. Finalize (user asks to publish / finalize)

1. Turn the current highest heading into `## vX.Y.Z – Short summary` (summary after the dash). Do not change the
   version strings.
2. Commit the finalize and create the git tag `vX.Y.Z`. Do not push unless asked.

## 2. Bump

Right after the tag (project decision, deviates from "wait until shipped"): add a new empty heading at the **end**
of `CHANGELOG.md` for the next version (patch bump unless the user names another), set it in `FyneApp.toml`
(`Version`, `Build = 1`) and `version.go`, commit as `chore: bump to vX.Y.Z`.
